\ A signal handler's user throw propagates out of the dispatcher, so the state that raise
\ wrote belongs to it and must survive: the error keeps its own type and message rather than
\ degrading to a bare user-thrown line. This is the one dispatch path the error-state shield
\ deliberately skips.
\
\ Same delivery shape as signal_handler_error_shielded.1z: `kill` delivers synchronously and
\ the following `drop` is the safe point that runs the handler.

use "os/signal" ;
use "posix" ;

SIGUSR1 [ drop f "handler boom" handler-error: make-error throw ] on-signal

getpid SIGUSR1 unmake-signal kill drop
